{"name":"Cashmere","hex":"#d1b399","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"Cashmere","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Proper noun","definitions":["Archaic spelling of Kashmir.","A city in Washington state, United States."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A breed of goat (Capra aegagrus hircus) raised for its hair."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/Cashmere"}],"entries":[{"title":"Cashmere wool","blocks":[{"text":"Cashmere wool, usually simply known as cashmere, is a fiber obtained from cashmere goats, pashmina goats, and some other breeds of goat. It has been used to make yarn, textiles and clothing for hundreds of years. Cashmere is closely associated with the Kashmir shawl, the word \"cashmere\" deriving from an anglicization of Kashmir, when the Kashmir shawl reached Europe in the 19th century. Both the soft undercoat and the guard hairs may be used; the softer hair is reserved for textiles, while the coarse guard hair is used for brushes and other non-apparel purposes. Cashmere is a hygroscopic fiber, absorbing and releasing water from the air based on the surrounding environment. This helps regulate the body in both warm and cool temperatures."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/01/Kaschmirschal_1.jpg/330px-Kaschmirschal_1.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Cashmere_wool"},{"title":"Cashmere goat","blocks":[{"text":"A cashmere goat is a type of goat that produces cashmere wool, the goat's fine, soft, downy, winter undercoat, in commercial quality and quantity. This undercoat grows as the days get shorter and is associated with an outer coat of coarse hair, which is present all the year and is called guard hair. Most common goat breeds, including dairy goats, grow this two-coated fleece but cashmere breeds have been selected for quality and quantity of their undercoat."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d8/Black_cashmere_goat_doe.jpg/330px-Black_cashmere_goat_doe.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Cashmere_goat"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/7b/Pashmina_goats.jpg/500px-Pashmina_goats.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/7b/Pashmina_goats.jpg/500px-Pashmina_goats.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Pashmina goats, Ladakh, India","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3APashmina_goats.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/83/Cashmeregoat_shearing.png/250px-Cashmeregoat_shearing.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/8/83/Cashmeregoat_shearing.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/83/Cashmeregoat_shearing.png/250px-Cashmeregoat_shearing.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Cashmere shearing. Corindhap, Australia.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ACashmeregoat_shearing.png"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/22/Shawl_makers_in_Kashmir_%281867%29.jpg/500px-Shawl_makers_in_Kashmir_%281867%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/22/Shawl_makers_in_Kashmir_%281867%29.jpg/500px-Shawl_makers_in_Kashmir_%281867%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"An 1867 William Simpson painting depicting men manufacturing shawls using pashm wool","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AShawl_makers_in_Kashmir_(1867).jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/5f/Cashmere_Factory_Gobi_26.JPG/500px-Cashmere_Factory_Gobi_26.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/5f/Cashmere_Factory_Gobi_26.JPG/1280px-Cashmere_Factory_Gobi_26.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/5f/Cashmere_Factory_Gobi_26.JPG/500px-Cashmere_Factory_Gobi_26.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Cashmere factory in Ulaanbaatar","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ACashmere_Factory_Gobi_26.JPG"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c9/Boy%27s_Frock_LACMA_M.2007.211.88_%281_of_10%29.jpg/500px-Boy%27s_Frock_LACMA_M.2007.211.88_%281_of_10%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c9/Boy%27s_Frock_LACMA_M.2007.211.88_%281_of_10%29.jpg/1280px-Boy%27s_Frock_LACMA_M.2007.211.88_%281_of_10%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c9/Boy%27s_Frock_LACMA_M.2007.211.88_%281_of_10%29.jpg/500px-Boy%27s_Frock_LACMA_M.2007.211.88_%281_of_10%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"A boy's frock produced c. 1855 in Kashmir; cashmere wool twill with silk embroidery and silk tassels.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ABoy's_Frock_LACMA_M.2007.211.88_(1_of_10).jpg"}],"sounds":{}}}